		<item>
		<title>Nascent Re issues $36m across Plymouth / Warwick preferred share insurance-linked securities</title>
		<link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-36m-across-plymouth-warwick-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=nascent-re-issues-36m-across-plymouth-warwick-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Steve Evans]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 07:00:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Insurance Linked Investments]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Collateralized reinsurance]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Insurance linked securities]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[insurance management]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Insurance-linked investments]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Nascent Group]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Nascent Re]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance linked investment]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurtech]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Transformer]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.artemis.bm/?p=151101</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Nascent Re Ltd. a licensed reinsurance transformer owned and operated by Bermuda-based Nascent Group, has issued another $36 million of preferred share insurance-linked securities, across two series named Plymouth and Warwick. These are the fifth and sixth individual issuances of ILS securities from Nascent Re that we&#8217;ve reported on, with all six seen to-date being [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-36m-across-plymouth-warwick-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities/">Nascent Re issues $36m across Plymouth / Warwick preferred share insurance-linked securities</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Nascent Re Ltd. a licensed reinsurance transformer owned and operated by Bermuda-based Nascent Group, has issued another $36 million of preferred share insurance-linked securities, across two series named Plymouth and Warwick.<br />
<span id="more-151101"></span><br />
<img decoding="async" data-attachment-id="108317" data-permalink="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-hires-de-klerk-for-catastrophe-bond-and-spv-management/attachment/nascent-group-logo/" data-orig-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo.png" data-orig-size="700,388" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="nascent-group-logo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo.png" class="alignright wp-image-108317" src="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo.png" alt="nascent-group-logo" width="360" height="200" srcset="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo.png 700w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo-300x166.png 300w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo-200x111.png 200w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/nascent-group-logo-350x194.png 350w" sizes="(max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />These are the fifth and sixth individual issuances of ILS securities from Nascent Re that we&#8217;ve reported on, with all six seen to-date being in preferred shares form, likely representing some kind of collateralized reinsurance or private ILS arrangement.</p>
<p>Nascent Group is a technology-driven insurance management, ILS servicing and reinsurance transformation specialist, with Nascent Re being its transformer vehicle.</p>
<p>The Nascent Re structure enables re/insurers and investors to transact reinsurance on a collateralized basis, through a managed and outsourced risk transformation platform.</p>
<p>While the six issuances of preferred share ILS we&#8217;ve seen from Nascent Re indicate growing traction in the market, it&#8217;s likely the structure has facilitated many more similar collateralized reinsurance or ILS arrangements in its history that we haven&#8217;t seen.</p>
<p>The first issuance of listed insurance-linked securities from Nascent Re emerged earlier this year in March 2026, with <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-its-first-listed-insurance-linked-securities-e10m-ofs-re-preferred-shares/">a €10 million tranche of OFS Re Series 2026-001 preferred shares issued</a>.</p>
<p>Then in August, <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-23-5m-telford-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities/">we saw Nascent Re issuing $23.5 million of preferred shares through a segregated account named Telford</a>, the second and still the largest single ILS issuance we’ve seen so far from the structure.</p>
<p>Following that, in September, <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-20m-quinton-20m-stevenage-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities/">Nascent Re Ltd. issued US $20 million of preferred shares on behalf of a segregated account named Quinton and a further US $20 million of preferred shares on behalf of a segregated account named Stevenage</a>.</p>
<p>Now, we&#8217;ve learned that Nascent Re Ltd. has issued US $16 million of preferred shares on behalf of a segregated account named Plymouth and a further US $20 million of preferred shares on behalf of a segregated account named Warwick.</p>
<p>The $16 million tranche of Plymouth preferred shares are scheduled for maturity on June 30th 2027, so perhaps representing a roughly one-year collateralized reinsurance or retrocession arrangement, while the $20 million of Warwick preferred shares are due for maturity on December 15th 2026, so could represent a transaction that runs through the wind season, given the timing.</p>
<p>As ever, we don&#8217;t know the actual inception dates of the underlying risk transfer arrangements, only having visibility as the preferred shares get listed.</p>
<p>All $36 million of preferred shares from the Plymouth and Warwick segregated accounts of Nascent Re have been privately placed with qualifying investors and listed on the Bermuda Stock Exchange (BSX) as insurance-linked securities.</p>
<p>Being another issuance of preferred shares, rather than principal-at-risk notes, it again suggests the underlying structure could be a quota share reinsurance or retrocessional arrangement, rather than excess-of-loss. However we cannot be certain.</p>
<p>With now six issuances of preferred share ILS securities seen, they total around US $110 million from the group of transactions.</p>
<p>Nascent Re Ltd., a Class 3 licensed Bermuda insurer, facilitates the matching of reinsurance and retrocessional risk and capital between sponsors and investors or ILS fund managers, providing a way for traditional insurance or reinsurance clients to efficiently transact with the capital markets.</p>
<p>Nascent Re can transform re/insurance related risks into securities for investors and ILS funds, so providing a conduit to the capital markets for Nascent clients.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nascent-re-issues-36m-across-plymouth-warwick-preferred-share-insurance-linked-securities/">Nascent Re issues $36m across Plymouth / Warwick preferred share insurance-linked securities</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">151101</post-id>	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Stand hires former Nephila exec Landi as CFO, raises $70 Million Series C</title>
		<link>https://www.artemis.bm/news/stand-hires-former-nephila-exec-landi-as-cfo-raises-70-million-series-c/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=stand-hires-former-nephila-exec-landi-as-cfo-raises-70-million-series-c</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Steve Evans]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:50:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Reinsurance News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Insurtech - Insurance technology fintech in reinsurance & ILS]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[People Moves]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[reinsurance]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.artemis.bm/?p=151080</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Stand, a licensed insurance producer with a focus on insuring property in catastrophe-exposed regions, has announced the hiring of former Nephila Capital executive Tony Landi as its Chief Financial Officer, with a remit to ensure the right reinsurance capital is there to support the company as it grows. Stand has grown from $1 billion of [&#8230;]</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/stand-hires-former-nephila-exec-landi-as-cfo-raises-70-million-series-c/">Stand hires former Nephila exec Landi as CFO, raises $70 Million Series C</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This content is copyright to <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.artemis.bm</a> and should not appear anywhere else, or an infringement has occurred.</p>
<p>Stand, a licensed insurance producer with a focus on insuring property in catastrophe-exposed regions, has announced the hiring of former Nephila Capital executive Tony Landi as its Chief Financial Officer, with a remit to ensure the right reinsurance capital is there to support the company as it grows.<br />
<span id="more-151080"></span><br />
<img decoding="async" data-attachment-id="151083" data-permalink="https://www.artemis.bm/news/stand-hires-former-nephila-exec-landi-as-cfo-raises-70-million-series-c/attachment/stand-logo/" data-orig-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo.png" data-orig-size="720,440" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="stand-logo" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo.png" class="alignright wp-image-151083" src="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo.png" alt="stand-logo" width="360" height="220" srcset="https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo.png 720w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo-300x183.png 300w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo-200x122.png 200w, https://www.artemis.bm/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/stand-logo-350x214.png 350w" sizes="(max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" />Stand has grown from $1 billion of property insured a year ago to now $10 billion and today announced the completion of a Series C fund raise that secured the company $70 million  at a $1 billion valuation.</p>
<p>Backers in the round included leader Saga Ventures, with participation from Lowercarbon, Eclipse, Equal Ventures, Inspired Capital, Neotribe, and Jackson Square Ventures, among others.</p>
<p>Stand has a mission to &#8220;to insure all the world&#8217;s resilient property, by making homes safer and thus insurance cheaper,&#8221; and part of that will inevitably be ensuring it has the most efficient reinsurance capital in place.</p>
<p>Stand uses its Stand World Model to create a digital representation of every home it aims to insurer, simulating how it will perform under catastrophe conditions, from fire, wind, and other disasters. The model accounts for home construction, surroundings, and the weather or catastrophe conditions it faces.</p>
<p>&#8220;Instead of waiting decades for history to reveal what works, Stand pulls the future forward. It shows exactly what makes a specific home vulnerable and the most cost-effective ways to protect it,&#8221; Stand said.</p>
<p>The company believes this will mean safer homes, given the resilience angle as it helps homeowners understand how they can improve it, while delivering cheaper insurance over the long-term and making coverage more durable.</p>
<p>&#8220;Disasters follow the laws of physics, and insurance should too,&#8221; explained Dan Preston, co-founder and CEO of Stand. &#8220;If your home is resilient, you should be rewarded with a low premium and never have to worry about losing your coverage. We want to insure every resilient property in the world, and help make every property safe.&#8221;</p>
<p>Stand already counts specialist insurance-linked securities investment manager Nephila Capital as one of its reinsurers and has now hired a former Nephila employee.</p>
<p>Tony Landi has joined the company as Chief Financial Officer, most recently having been Head of Strategic Growth at Nephila.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/nephila-hires-former-openly-everest-exec-landi-as-head-of-strategic-growth/">Landi had joined Nephila as Head of Strategic Growth for the firm’s Nephila Advisors investor relations and US business development division in early 2026</a>.</p>
<p>Prior to that, Landi was Head of Reinsurance &amp; Capital Management at Openly and Head of Portfolio Management at Everest Re.</p>
<p>At Stand, Landi will be tasked with leading finance, reinsurance, capital markets, and growth strategy as the company expands.</p>
<p>&#8220;What drew me to Stand is the depth of the team, with real experts in physics, underwriting, and product working on the same problem,&#8221; explained Landi. &#8220;My job is to make sure that as Stand grows, the capital is there to support it, from our investors and our reinsurance partners alike.</p>
<p>&#8220;We&#8217;ll do that by building diversified, resilient portfolios and matching risk and returns to capital appetite.&#8221;</p>
<p>The company has also hired Drew Saad as President of Property &amp; Casualty, who joins after most recently being the Chief Underwriting Officer at PURE Insurance.</p>
<p>&#8220;The companies that reshape a market for decades are the ones that identify a fundamentally better way to understand risk, and Stand has done that for the homes exposed to natural disasters,&#8221; Saad commented. &#8220;With the science already in place, the opportunity now is to build an insurance operation that matches it and scales it to every market that needs it. That is the work I have spent my career preparing for, and it is why I joined Stand.&#8221;</p>
<p>Stand is another example of a tech-forward underwriter of catastrophe exposed properties and as such its access to efficient reinsurance capital will be critical. The hiring of Landi brings onboard expertise in the capital markets and ILS space, which should benefit the company as it establishes more risk capital partnerships over-time.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.artemis.bm/news/stand-hires-former-nephila-exec-landi-as-cfo-raises-70-million-series-c/">Stand hires former Nephila exec Landi as CFO, raises $70 Million Series C</a> was published by: <a href="https://www.artemis.bm">www.Artemis.bm</a><br />
Our <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/">catastrophe bond deal directory</a><br />
Sign up for <a href="https://www.artemis.bm/e-newsletter/">our free weekly email newsletter here</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
